1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,933
You just finished a lesson

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:03,533
You wrote three pages of notes

3
00:00:03,566 --> 00:00:05,066
You marked a lot of key points

4
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:06,366
A friend casually asks you

5
00:00:06,366 --> 00:00:08,000
What was that lesson really about

6
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:09,233
You open your mouth

7
00:00:09,233 --> 00:00:10,800
And suddenly only a few words remain

8
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:11,766
Method

9
00:00:11,766 --> 00:00:12,533
Model

10
00:00:12,533 --> 00:00:13,200
Cognition

11
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:14,133
Very important

12
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:15,366
And then nothing

13
00:00:15,433 --> 00:00:17,366
That second is actually very honest

14
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:18,966
It is not that you are bad at speaking

15
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,533
You are just discovering for the first time

16
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,633
That you mistook hearing for understanding

17
00:00:22,733 --> 00:00:24,733
The sharpest part of the Feynman technique

18
00:00:24,766 --> 00:00:26,466
Is not some magic trick

19
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:28,233
It is just taking a blank sheet of paper

20
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:30,266
And bringing out the things you seem to understand

21
00:00:30,333 --> 00:00:31,766
One by one

22
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:33,233
Letting them stand under the light

23
00:00:33,233 --> 00:00:33,933
If they can stand

24
00:00:33,933 --> 00:00:34,900
They are yours

25
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:35,666
If they cannot

26
00:00:35,733 --> 00:00:37,666
They are still someone elses words

27
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:40,033
The easiest trap in learning

28
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:41,300
Is not having a bad memory

29
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:43,000
It is seeing something too many times

30
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:44,600
And mistaking familiarity for understanding

31
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:46,833
You have definitely seen this scene

32
00:00:47,333 --> 00:00:48,366
At a book club

33
00:00:48,433 --> 00:00:49,733
Everyone sits in a circle

34
00:00:49,766 --> 00:00:50,566
Someone asks

35
00:00:50,766 --> 00:00:53,266
What inspired you most in this book

36
00:00:53,533 --> 00:00:55,500
You clearly underlined the whole book

37
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:56,800
And folded several corners

38
00:00:56,966 --> 00:00:58,133
But when it is your turn

39
00:00:58,233 --> 00:00:59,166
You can only say

40
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:00,633
I think it is quite deep

41
00:01:00,633 --> 00:01:01,833
It talks about human nature

42
00:01:01,833 --> 00:01:02,800
And choice

43
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:04,133
And long term thinking

44
00:01:04,333 --> 00:01:06,000
Even you feel guilty after saying it

45
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:07,433
Not because you did not read it

46
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:08,666
You really did read it

47
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:10,200
And not because the book is bad

48
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:11,800
The book may truly be good

49
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:12,766
The problem is

50
00:01:12,833 --> 00:01:15,166
When those sentences passed before your eyes

51
00:01:15,333 --> 00:01:16,566
You only nodded along

52
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,633
You did not turn them into your own words

53
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:20,600
That nodding is very deceptive

54
00:01:20,766 --> 00:01:21,933
The teacher explains smoothly

55
00:01:22,033 --> 00:01:23,200
The video is edited smoothly

56
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:24,466
The author writes smoothly

57
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:25,666
You sit there

58
00:01:25,766 --> 00:01:27,433
Follow his path once

59
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:29,266
And think you can walk it too

60
00:01:29,366 --> 00:01:30,833
But once you leave that path

61
00:01:30,833 --> 00:01:33,133
You immediately do not know where to step next

62
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:35,233
It is like watching someone fix a faucet

63
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:36,433
He picks up a wrench

64
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:37,366
Turns it twice

65
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:38,433
Replaces a washer

66
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:39,566
And the leak stops

67
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,366
You watch beside him and understand it clearly

68
00:01:41,433 --> 00:01:43,600
You may even think how hard can this be

69
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:45,600
Then when your faucet really breaks

70
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:46,800
You squat on the floor

71
00:01:46,833 --> 00:01:48,066
Holding the wrench

72
00:01:48,166 --> 00:01:50,466
And realize you were only watching the show

73
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:51,866
Learning is the same

74
00:01:51,966 --> 00:01:53,233
Understanding by watching is not ability

75
00:01:53,366 --> 00:01:54,633
Understanding by listening is not ability

76
00:01:54,766 --> 00:01:56,266
Saving it is even less ability

77
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,500
Whether you can explain something

78
00:01:58,500 --> 00:01:59,966
Is the first real inspection

79
00:02:00,133 --> 00:02:01,866
So being unable to explain is not shameful

80
00:02:01,966 --> 00:02:03,333
It is actually valuable

81
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:05,266
Because it turns a vague problem

82
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,133
Into a specific hole

83
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:08,366
You finally know

84
00:02:08,366 --> 00:02:10,366
It is not that you failed to understand the whole book

85
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,000
It is that this part did not connect

86
00:02:12,166 --> 00:02:13,833
It is not that the whole lesson was wasted

87
00:02:13,933 --> 00:02:16,266
It is that the example was too far from your life

88
00:02:16,366 --> 00:02:17,533
The real trouble

89
00:02:17,533 --> 00:02:18,933
Is not that you cannot explain it

90
00:02:18,966 --> 00:02:20,366
It is that you cannot explain it

91
00:02:20,366 --> 00:02:22,166
Yet still think you already understand

92
00:02:22,433 --> 00:02:24,433
When many people hear Feynman technique

93
00:02:24,733 --> 00:02:25,766
Their first reaction is

94
00:02:25,933 --> 00:02:28,000
Explain complex things to a child

95
00:02:28,233 --> 00:02:29,600
That sentence is of course not wrong

96
00:02:29,966 --> 00:02:31,000
But if you only remember that

97
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,366
It is easy to learn it the wrong way

98
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:33,833
You start thinking about

99
00:02:33,966 --> 00:02:35,133
How to say it beautifully

100
00:02:35,133 --> 00:02:36,566
How to give a good example

101
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:38,533
How to make others think you are impressive

102
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:40,000
But this Feynman method

103
00:02:40,033 --> 00:02:41,866
Is not meant to make you perform on stage

104
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,433
It is meant to expose the gap

105
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:45,100
Exposure sounds unpleasant

106
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:46,033
But it is very accurate

107
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:47,366
You take a sheet of paper

108
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,766
Write down a word you think you understand

109
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:50,833
For example compound interest

110
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:52,033
For example opportunity cost

111
00:02:52,033 --> 00:02:53,000
For example inflation

112
00:02:53,033 --> 00:02:54,800
For example the Feynman technique itself

113
00:02:54,966 --> 00:02:56,233
Then do not open the book

114
00:02:56,233 --> 00:02:57,366
And do not look at your notes

115
00:02:57,433 --> 00:02:59,633
Just imagine someone across from you has never heard of it

116
00:02:59,966 --> 00:03:01,200
You need to use a few plain words

117
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,366
To make it clear

118
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,433
Soon you will hit a spot

119
00:03:04,533 --> 00:03:05,566
Where your mouth stops

120
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:06,866
And your mind starts searching for words

121
00:03:07,033 --> 00:03:08,066
The more you search the weaker you feel

122
00:03:08,333 --> 00:03:09,866
At this moment do not rush to blame yourself

123
00:03:09,966 --> 00:03:11,866
And do not quickly use the original text to save you

124
00:03:11,966 --> 00:03:12,833
First take a look

125
00:03:12,833 --> 00:03:14,466
At where exactly you got stuck

126
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:15,433
Is the concept unclear

127
00:03:15,433 --> 00:03:16,633
Is the example not connecting

128
00:03:16,766 --> 00:03:18,366
Or did you only memorize a conclusion

129
00:03:18,366 --> 00:03:20,066
Without knowing why it holds

130
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:21,833
For example you say you understand compound interest

131
00:03:21,933 --> 00:03:23,500
Can you explain without formulas

132
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:25,300
Why the longer time passes

133
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:26,666
The faster it suddenly grows later

134
00:03:26,966 --> 00:03:28,666
You say you understand opportunity cost

135
00:03:28,733 --> 00:03:30,133
Then can you explain clearly

136
00:03:30,133 --> 00:03:31,600
Why a free lecture

137
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:32,666
Can also be expensive

138
00:03:32,833 --> 00:03:34,200
You say you understand inflation

139
00:03:34,333 --> 00:03:35,600
Then can you explain clearly

140
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:36,833
Why your salary did not fall

141
00:03:36,833 --> 00:03:38,200
But life keeps getting tighter

142
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:39,533
If you cannot explain it

143
00:03:39,533 --> 00:03:40,666
It does not mean you are stupid

144
00:03:40,833 --> 00:03:42,366
It only means what you have right now

145
00:03:42,366 --> 00:03:43,466
Is not yet understanding

146
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:44,933
It is only a familiar word

147
00:03:45,133 --> 00:03:47,366
The truly useful part of the Feynman technique

148
00:03:47,366 --> 00:03:49,066
Is not training you to become a teacher

149
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:51,433
It is making you stop hiding behind jargon

150
00:03:51,633 --> 00:03:53,000
When many people cannot explain clearly

151
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,866
They start covering it with big words

152
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:55,733
Structure

153
00:03:55,733 --> 00:03:56,366
System

154
00:03:56,366 --> 00:03:57,033
Long term

155
00:03:57,033 --> 00:03:57,800
Foundational

156
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,233
A pile of words drops down

157
00:03:59,233 --> 00:04:00,333
It sounds full

158
00:04:00,433 --> 00:04:02,166
But inside it may be empty

159
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:04,233
The blank paper is not intimidated by these words

160
00:04:04,233 --> 00:04:05,333
If you cannot write it

161
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,633
It stays empty

162
00:04:06,766 --> 00:04:08,800
Blank space is sometimes more honest than notes

163
00:04:08,966 --> 00:04:11,066
You will also meet this at work

164
00:04:11,333 --> 00:04:12,266
In an afternoon meeting

165
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,766
Your manager asks you to explain

166
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:15,633
Why this proposal should be done this way

167
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:18,033
You clearly read a pile of materials that morning

168
00:04:18,133 --> 00:04:19,800
And your mind still has many screenshots

169
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,000
But once you open your mouth

170
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:21,933
Only one sentence remains

171
00:04:22,033 --> 00:04:23,633
The industry trend is like this

172
00:04:23,766 --> 00:04:25,466
Customer needs are changing too

173
00:04:25,533 --> 00:04:27,066
We need to plan ahead

174
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:28,566
These words are not wrong

175
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:30,000
But they are too light

176
00:04:30,033 --> 00:04:31,366
So light anyone can say them

177
00:04:31,566 --> 00:04:33,000
A colleague asks one more question

178
00:04:33,133 --> 00:04:34,566
Where exactly is the change

179
00:04:34,566 --> 00:04:35,800
Why do it now

180
00:04:35,833 --> 00:04:37,366
What do we lose if we do not

181
00:04:37,366 --> 00:04:38,633
You immediately start circling around

182
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:40,033
What shows up then

183
00:04:40,033 --> 00:04:41,433
Is not your speaking problem

184
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:43,866
It is whether you really chewed through the material

185
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:45,666
What many people call learning

186
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,566
Is actually moving other peoples judgments

187
00:04:47,566 --> 00:04:48,966
To the edge of their own mouth

188
00:04:49,166 --> 00:04:51,233
But when they really have to own that sentence

189
00:04:51,333 --> 00:04:52,533
It cannot stand

190
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:54,633
Learning things is too easy now

191
00:04:54,833 --> 00:04:56,233
Easy enough to be a little dangerous

192
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:57,766
You swipe to a video

193
00:04:57,966 --> 00:04:59,433
And feel it is so right

194
00:04:59,466 --> 00:05:00,266
Save it

195
00:05:00,566 --> 00:05:01,766
You see an article

196
00:05:01,833 --> 00:05:03,533
And feel it will surely be useful later

197
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:04,400
Save it

198
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:05,633
You buy a course

199
00:05:05,833 --> 00:05:07,666
And feel you will miss out if you do not buy now

200
00:05:07,733 --> 00:05:08,533
Place the order

201
00:05:08,966 --> 00:05:10,800
Every action looks like effort

202
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,800
But they may just be moving things into a warehouse

203
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:16,366
If your home is piled with many delivery boxes

204
00:05:16,633 --> 00:05:18,733
And every box says useful on the outside

205
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:20,166
Some say self discipline

206
00:05:20,233 --> 00:05:21,533
Some say wealth

207
00:05:21,633 --> 00:05:22,866
Some say expression

208
00:05:22,933 --> 00:05:24,200
Some say learning

209
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:25,466
You look at them

210
00:05:25,533 --> 00:05:27,233
And feel you own a lot

211
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:28,633
But as long as you do not open them

212
00:05:28,766 --> 00:05:30,600
They are still only boxes

213
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:32,000
Knowledge is the same

214
00:05:32,133 --> 00:05:33,033
If you have not explained it

215
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:33,933
Not used it

216
00:05:33,966 --> 00:05:36,000
Not used it to explain your own life

217
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:37,333
Then it has not been opened yet

218
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:39,933
This is why many people learn more and feel more confused

219
00:05:40,166 --> 00:05:41,600
Not because they learned too little

220
00:05:41,733 --> 00:05:43,400
But because too much comes in

221
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:44,466
And too little goes out

222
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:47,066
The mind is like an unsorted saved folder

223
00:05:47,333 --> 00:05:48,200
It has everything

224
00:05:48,333 --> 00:05:49,600
But when you really need it

225
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:50,733
You cannot find anything

226
00:05:50,966 --> 00:05:52,200
You want to write a paragraph

227
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:54,466
And find your mind full of other peoples punchlines

228
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:56,033
You want to explain a problem

229
00:05:56,333 --> 00:05:58,333
And find you can only quote the original words

230
00:05:58,500 --> 00:05:59,833
You want to make a decision

231
00:05:59,966 --> 00:06:01,766
And find those models all feel familiar

232
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:04,466
But none can land on the thing in front of you

233
00:06:04,633 --> 00:06:05,800
This is not learning

234
00:06:05,833 --> 00:06:06,833
This is hoarding

235
00:06:06,966 --> 00:06:08,833
And it is very respectable hoarding

236
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,366
Because books look respectable

237
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:11,633
Courses look respectable

238
00:06:11,733 --> 00:06:12,933
Notes look respectable

239
00:06:12,933 --> 00:06:14,533
Saved folders look respectable too

240
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:15,700
They make you feel

241
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:17,100
I did not waste my time

242
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:18,066
I am getting better

243
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:20,966
But if something has never been explained by you

244
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,466
And never been used by you

245
00:06:22,633 --> 00:06:24,433
It is very hard for it to really change you

246
00:06:24,633 --> 00:06:25,800
This Feynman thing

247
00:06:25,966 --> 00:06:28,400
Is like placing a table at the warehouse door

248
00:06:28,533 --> 00:06:30,200
Every time you move in a box

249
00:06:30,233 --> 00:06:31,066
Open it first

250
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:32,933
See what is actually inside

251
00:06:32,933 --> 00:06:33,800
See whether it can be used

252
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:35,566
See whether you can explain it to others

253
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,666
If after opening it you find you do not understand

254
00:06:37,733 --> 00:06:38,666
That is also good

255
00:06:38,833 --> 00:06:41,033
At least it no longer pretends to be your inventory

256
00:06:41,300 --> 00:06:42,133
Many times

257
00:06:42,333 --> 00:06:44,033
When a person truly becomes clearer

258
00:06:44,033 --> 00:06:46,133
It is not because they saved another opinion

259
00:06:46,166 --> 00:06:49,333
But because they finally deleted many pretty words they could not explain

260
00:06:49,533 --> 00:06:51,666
There is another hidden cost to this

261
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:53,866
It makes people less and less willing to speak

262
00:06:54,033 --> 00:06:55,433
Because deep down you know

263
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:57,166
You are not actually that certain

264
00:06:57,233 --> 00:06:59,033
So you speak less in group chats

265
00:06:59,133 --> 00:07:00,600
Express less in meetings

266
00:07:00,766 --> 00:07:02,833
You see a topic and clearly have thoughts

267
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:04,933
But in the end you just like it and scroll away

268
00:07:05,033 --> 00:07:06,400
It is not that you have no view

269
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:09,366
It is that most of your views still sit inside other peoples sentences

270
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:11,066
And have not been opened by your own hands

271
00:07:11,233 --> 00:07:12,366
Things you have not opened

272
00:07:12,533 --> 00:07:13,866
Make you afraid they will break when shown

273
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:15,366
The more afraid you are

274
00:07:15,433 --> 00:07:16,733
The more you keep saving

275
00:07:16,733 --> 00:07:17,766
Keep taking classes

276
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:19,400
Keep waiting until you are ready

277
00:07:19,566 --> 00:07:20,966
But being ready

278
00:07:21,033 --> 00:07:22,766
Often does not arrive by itself

279
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:24,700
It grows little by little

280
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:26,166
After you mess up a few explanations

281
00:07:26,333 --> 00:07:28,666
So this video is not telling you

282
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:31,266
To become a learning machine from today

283
00:07:31,533 --> 00:07:34,166
Nor to write a book report for every book

284
00:07:34,266 --> 00:07:35,066
No need

285
00:07:35,433 --> 00:07:36,433
Most content

286
00:07:36,433 --> 00:07:37,666
Can simply pass after you see it

287
00:07:37,933 --> 00:07:39,200
Just let it go

288
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:41,033
But if there is something

289
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:42,433
You truly want to master

290
00:07:42,633 --> 00:07:45,066
And truly hope it helps your judgment later

291
00:07:45,233 --> 00:07:47,000
Then do not rush to the next lesson

292
00:07:47,366 --> 00:07:49,133
Tonight find a sheet of paper first

293
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:50,400
Write down one word

294
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:51,433
Just one

295
00:07:51,433 --> 00:07:52,433
Do not get greedy

296
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,566
For example inflation

297
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:54,566
For example compound interest

298
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:55,966
For example sunk cost

299
00:07:56,133 --> 00:07:58,300
For example the idea you just saved

300
00:07:58,300 --> 00:08:00,200
Then explain it in three sentences

301
00:08:00,366 --> 00:08:01,966
Do not use the original sentence from the book

302
00:08:02,133 --> 00:08:03,733
Do not use the teachers example

303
00:08:03,766 --> 00:08:05,366
Do not say this is very complicated

304
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:07,033
Just imagine you are at the dinner table

305
00:08:07,033 --> 00:08:09,033
Explaining it to someone who has never heard of it

306
00:08:09,233 --> 00:08:10,133
First sentence

307
00:08:10,233 --> 00:08:11,666
What exactly is it saying

308
00:08:11,766 --> 00:08:12,666
Second sentence

309
00:08:12,833 --> 00:08:14,166
Why does it happen

310
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:15,366
Third sentence

311
00:08:15,533 --> 00:08:17,600
What does it have to do with my life

312
00:08:17,633 --> 00:08:19,166
If all three sentences flow

313
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:21,000
Then find your own example

314
00:08:21,133 --> 00:08:23,533
For example why you cannot bear to refund a course

315
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:26,566
Why your salary did not shrink but money feels short

316
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:28,533
Why a free event

317
00:08:28,533 --> 00:08:30,433
Ended up tiring you out for a whole day

318
00:08:30,566 --> 00:08:32,566
Once you can change it into your own example

319
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:34,766
That knowledge has finally touched you

320
00:08:34,766 --> 00:08:36,800
You can also explain it to a specific person

321
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,366
For example to a coworker

322
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:39,433
To your partner

323
00:08:39,433 --> 00:08:40,866
To a friend at the dinner table

324
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,200
No need to be formal

325
00:08:42,300 --> 00:08:44,633
And no need to say let me share a knowledge point

326
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:46,066
Just like chatting

327
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:47,800
Put it into a small thing

328
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:50,133
Why you recently want to cancel a membership

329
00:08:50,333 --> 00:08:52,333
Why you do not want to buy another course

330
00:08:52,533 --> 00:08:54,200
Why your salary rose a little

331
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,666
But money feels even tighter

332
00:08:55,833 --> 00:08:57,966
If after listening the other person can say

333
00:08:57,966 --> 00:08:58,600
Oh

334
00:08:58,600 --> 00:08:59,966
So that is how it works

335
00:09:00,333 --> 00:09:03,133
It means the concept finally came down from the book

336
00:09:03,166 --> 00:09:04,433
And landed in life

337
00:09:04,433 --> 00:09:06,333
If you cannot write the third sentence

338
00:09:06,366 --> 00:09:07,366
Do not feel embarrassed

339
00:09:07,533 --> 00:09:09,200
That is exactly the part you need to fill

340
00:09:09,333 --> 00:09:10,933
Not reading it all again from the start

341
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:12,566
But going back to patch this hole

342
00:09:12,733 --> 00:09:13,600
Look up one sentence

343
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:14,666
Change one example

344
00:09:14,733 --> 00:09:15,966
Explain it again

345
00:09:16,133 --> 00:09:17,500
The scariest thing in learning

346
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:18,266
Is not being slow

347
00:09:18,433 --> 00:09:20,200
It is that you keep turning pages forward

348
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:23,133
But never check whether the last page became yours

349
00:09:23,166 --> 00:09:25,000
Next time you finish a book

350
00:09:25,166 --> 00:09:27,233
Or swipe to a video that feels very reasonable

351
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:28,633
Do not rush to say

352
00:09:28,633 --> 00:09:29,933
Saved for later

353
00:09:30,133 --> 00:09:31,933
And do not rush to forward it to others

354
00:09:32,033 --> 00:09:32,966
Take a sheet of paper

355
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:33,966
Write three sentences

356
00:09:34,133 --> 00:09:35,766
Explain it to someone who has never heard it

357
00:09:35,766 --> 00:09:37,633
If you get stuck while explaining

358
00:09:37,633 --> 00:09:38,400
Do not rush

359
00:09:38,433 --> 00:09:39,800
That does not mean you are hopeless

360
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:42,966
It means knowledge has stopped hiding behind someone elses sentences

361
00:09:43,033 --> 00:09:44,633
It finally stands in front of you

362
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:45,800
And lets you see clearly

363
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:46,966
Where it is still empty

364
00:09:46,966 --> 00:09:48,433
That moment feels a little uncomfortable

365
00:09:48,533 --> 00:09:49,566
But it is also good

366
00:09:49,566 --> 00:09:51,333
Because what truly belongs to you

367
00:09:51,566 --> 00:09:53,733
Often begins with that discomfort
